Key Takeaways

- Nmap is used to discover hosts and services on a network.
- A host is any device connected to a network.
- Ports allow different services to communicate.
- Open ports accept connections.
- Closed ports are reachable but not in use.
- Filtered ports are usually protected by a firewall or packet filtering.
- Service detection helps identify the software running on open ports.
- TryHackMe provides hands-on labs to practice cybersecurity skills.

